#%PAM-1.0
# polkit prompts (the admin dialogs from Noctalia). A fingerprint or a YubiKey touch each prove the
# user is at the keyboard, so either one is enough; the password is only the fallback.
#
# pam_fprintd goes first, as in /etc/pam.d/sudo. pam_u2f needs a registered key
# (`mise run register-u2f`); with none registered it is skipped, so the password still works.
# Do not add nouserok to pam_u2f: with `sufficient` it would turn "no key registered" into success.
# The fingerprint wait is short (one try, 5 s) so a YubiKey touch is reachable without waiting out
# fprintd's default 30 s, and a crashing fprintd does not hold up the prompt.
auth       sufficient   pam_fprintd.so   max-tries=1 timeout=5
auth       sufficient   pam_u2f.so       cue
auth       include      system-auth
account    include      system-auth
password   include      system-auth
session    include      system-auth
